# Experimental 120 MHz SPI flash (vs the default 80 MHz) - ESP32-S3 test variant:
#   AIOTEDGE_VARIANTS=flash120 AIOTEDGE_S3_FLASH=16mb idf.py -B build_f120 build
#
# IMPORTANT - NOT usable on the default S3 camera board (octal PSRAM @ 80 MHz): the S3 ties flash and
# PSRAM to the shared MSPI, and IDF rejects the flash@120 + octal-PSRAM@80 combination at COMPILE time
# (static assert "FLASH and PSRAM Mode configuration are not supported": MSPI core_clock/psram_clock
# must be a power of 2; 240/80 = 3). Octal PSRAM cannot be moved to 120 MHz here either. So on this
# board flash stays at 80 MHz - this is a compile-time block, not a runtime fallback.
#
# This variant is therefore only for a QUAD-PSRAM or no-PSRAM ESP32-S3. There:
#  - SPI_FLASH_HPM_AUTO probes the chip at boot and engages 120 MHz only if it's in IDF's supported
#    table (the GD25Q128 / JEDEC 0xC84018 used here IS supported); an unsupported chip falls back to
#    80 MHz automatically. The 2nd-stage bootloader stays at 80 MHz; HPM bumps to 120 at runtime.
#  - 120 MHz flash is an EXPERIMENTAL IDF feature (temperature-stability caveats) - validate on
#    hardware, never ship as a default.
CONFIG_ESPTOOLPY_FLASHFREQ_120M=y
CONFIG_SPI_FLASH_HPM_AUTO=y
